  "id": "COMPOUND:23430 - PROTEIN:5788",
  "verbalization": "Caerulomycin A is implicated in the biological pathway leading to SNB-78 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Caerulomycin A directly targets VMRC-LCP, which in turn is a target of Cocosamide B and Maplexin A, all of which ultimately direct their activity to SNB-78. This indicates a potential hierarchical relationship where Caerulomycin A may act as a precursor or modulator in the signaling cascade that leads to SNB-78. The shared target SNB-78 across multiple pathways suggests a possible functional overlap or regulatory mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular network involved, emphasizing the need for further investigation into the precise mechanisms by which Caerulomycin A influences SNB-78.",
